  "id": "Compound::DB00972 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Ahlci, Azelastine, and Cyp2b6 are connected through a series of molecular interactions that suggest a potential role in drug metabolism. Azelastine, a histamine H1 receptor antagonist, is included in the class of compounds that interact with the histamine system, and it is linked to Cyp2b6 through a pathway involving arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. This suggests that Azelastine may influence Cyp2b6's function, possibly by modulating its activity in metabolic processes. Additionally, Azelastine is also linked to Cyp2b6 through its inclusion in the class of histamine H1 receptor antagonists, which includes Carbinoxamine and Diphenhydramine, both of which bind to Cyp2b6. These findings indicate that Azelastine may act as a modulator of Cyp2b6, potentially affecting its role in the metabolism of arachidonic acid and other substrates. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on Cyp2b6 for the metabolic conversion of arachidonic acid, with Azelastine serving as a regulator of this pathway.",
